  <!-- SECTION 5: FAQS & COMMUNITY RESOURCES \(SWAPPED TO BE BEFORE SCALE & METRICS\) -->
  <section id="nam-faqs" aria-labelledby="nam-faqs-title">
    <div class="mgdb-section-heading">
      <div><h2 id="nam-faqs-title">FAQs</h2></div>
    </div>

    <div class="mgdb-panel">
<div class="mgdb-card-grid nam-faqs-grid">
      <!-- FAQ 1: What is NAM -->
      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-info">Concept</span>
        <h3>What is Nested Association Mapping?</h3>
        <p>Nested Association Mapping \(NAM\) combines the advantages of linkage analysis \(high statistical power\) with genome-wide association studies \(high genetic resolution\). A common reference parent \(B73\) was crossed to 25 diverse founder lines, and 200 recombinant inbred lines \(RILs\) were generated per family to create ~5,000 lines with high historical and recent recombination density.</p>
      </article>

      <!-- FAQ 2: Annotation IDs -->
      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-warn">Annotation Note</span>
        <h3>Preliminary vs Official Gene Identifiers</h3>
        <p>The NAM founder assemblies were initially released with preliminary gene annotations \(e.g., <code>Zm00018a.1</code> for B97\). The official annotations \(e.g., <code>Zm00018ab.1</code>\) replaced the preliminary models with improved evidence-based structures and sequential numbering. Use the cross-reference translation files linked in the table above to map between versions.</p>
      </article>

      <!-- FAQ 3: Ordering Seed -->
      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <span class="mgdb-pill mgdb-pill-ok">Seed Ordering</span>
        <h3>How to Order NAM RIL Seed Lines</h3>
        <p>Seed packets for the NAM founder lines and the ~5,000 recombinant inbred lines are maintained and distributed by the <strong>Maize Genetics Cooperation Stock Center</strong>. You can place seed requests directly through the <a href="https://maizecoopsc.org/nam-rils.php" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Maize COOP Stock Center NAM Portal &#8599;</a> or browse individual stock records linked above.</p>
      </article>

      <!-- FAQ 4: Reporting Issues -->
      <article class="mgdb-card">
        <span class="mgdb-pill">Curation</span>
        <h3>Report Assembly or Gene Model Issues</h3>
        <p>If you encounter sequence anomalies, scaffold misorientations, or questionable gene annotations in any NAM assembly, you can submit an issue report directly to MaizeGDB curators via the <a href="/curation/GenomeIssue/edit">Genome Issue Curation Form &#8599;</a> to assist ongoing community curation.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </div>

  </section>

